1. e4 Nc6 2. d4 e5 3. d5 Nce7 { If you don't want to follow the general plan of the Linksspring you can try the King's Indian Defense Setup. The K.I.D. is an extremely popular opening and is very solid, so you can use the setup if you want. It's kind of a "system". Speaking of which, I have a study about Opening Systems: lichess.org/study/oBsew7N6 Please check it out! :) } 4. c4 d6 { All the moves that are designed into this system will be MARKED IN BLUE. } { [%csl Bd6][%cal Bd7d6] } 5. Nc3 g6 { [%csl Bg6][%cal Bg7g6] } 6. Bd3 Bg7 { [%csl Bg7][%cal Bf8g7] } 7. Nge2 f5 { This is an amazing move. If white captures, one pair of bishops can be exchanged. } { [%csl Bf5][%cal Ye4f5,Yc8f5,Bf7f5] } 8. O-O Nf6 { [%csl Bf6][%cal Bg8f6] } 9. Bd2 O-O { This is the ideal position you want to reach. } { [%csl Bg7,Bf6,Be7,Yg8,Bf8] } *


